    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABGEctNw",
      "title": "eth/076-080: Unichain Mainnet migration tasks",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1564,
      "body": "The Unichain Mainnet migration ceremony in five tasks, mirroring the Sepolia set (#1563) plus the L1Splitter handover that only exists on mainnet. eth/077 sets the OP Enterprise batcher and unsafe block signer (cutover steps 2 and 3), signed by the FoundationUpgradeSafe, which becomes the SystemConfig owner with eth/074 (#1560). eth/078 rotates the `SUPER_PERMISSIONED` (5) proposer (cutover step 4) and eth/080 points the OperatorFeeVault at the OPE cost recipient on L1; both are signed by the L1PAO.\n\nUnichain's Sequencer, Base and L1 fee vaults pay into Uniswap's FeeSplitter, whose L1-fee leg is the `Ownable2Step` L1Splitter `0x4300c0d3c0d3c0D3c0d3C0D3c0d3C0D3C0D30003`, owned by the alias of the Unichain SystemConfig owner Safe `0x9245d5D10AA8a842B31530De71EA86c0760Ca1b1`. eth/076 is that Safe starting the handover (`transferOwnership(alias(L1PAO))` via a portal deposit; named explicitly in `[addresses]` so it still resolves after eth/074 moves the SystemConfig), and eth/079 is the L1PAO accepting it and setting the recipient to the cost recipient with a 0.15 ETH minimum (eth/062 value). Both use `SetL1SplitterConfig` and the type-5 `SetDisputeGameArgs` support from #1562, which this PR is stacked on. The other splitter legs (`…0001`, `…0002`, `…0004`) are not touched.\n\nPlaceholders and open points: the OPE batcher, sequencer, proposer and cost recipient are `0xdead…0001` to `…0004`; the new L1Splitter owner (aliased L1PAO) is pending confirmation; the L1Splitter holds about 6 ETH below its 10 ETH minimum, which the lower minimum would let anyone withdraw to the new recipient; and the L1PAO tasks need the Maintenance Upgrade governance post. All tasks are DRAFT. Nonces are pinned to the live values on 2026-10-01 in stack order (eth/076 Unichain Safe 12, after eth/074; eth/077 FUS 73; eth/078-080 L1PAO 44-46 / FUS 74-76 / SC 71-73). Calldata was re-derived independently with `cast`, and `just simulate-stack` passes on both signing paths.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-01T10:13:22Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-15T22:11:47Z",
      "additions": 1139,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABIq0pvA",
      "title": "fix(sep): mark 112-113 executed and route stacked_simulation_sep alerts",
      "author": "OptimismBot",
      "number": 1578,
      "body": "Fixes the `stacked_simulation_sep` failure on `main` ([job 215474](https://circleci.com/gh/ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops/215474)):\n\n```\nStateOverrideManager: User-defined nonce (79) is less than current actual nonce (81) for contract: 0xDEe57160aAfCF04c34C887B5962D0a69676d3C8B in task config file: src/tasks/sep/112-op-sepolia-set-batcher/config.toml\n```\n\nBoth OP Sepolia OPE rotation tasks have executed, but they were still `READY TO SIGN`, so the stack kept simulating them against stale nonce pins.\n\n- **sep/112** executed in [0x3685ea82…](https://sepolia.etherscan.io/tx/0x3685ea82fda7ab9294dfa7552334f8524e8780a2916ee31968d68661d3e2d418) (FUS nonce 79). `SystemConfigProxy.batcherHash()` now returns `0x64EDa4F93314ECd619bd4f79D8d1F8112A4E6e16`.\n- **sep/113**: FUS approved in [0xb96382c4…](https://sepolia.etherscan.io/tx/0xb96382c4e047929d8725d59f62beed5987a20fd62ca84873c7aaeb7f543193f2) (FUS nonce 80), the Security Council approved in [0x62e3f92c…](https://sepolia.etherscan.io/tx/0x62e3f92c4c82adc3864b57166708b8992580d89a4b6ad6dc761022c60bb63caa), and the L1PAO executed in [0x09ddd356…](https://sepolia.etherscan.io/tx/0x09ddd356f37fef92897a577074d0e5766c417e00036aefb80d32b400db76e571) (L1PAO nonce 58 → 59). `DisputeGameFactory.gameArgs(5)` now contains proposer `0x9884C33C65111DA7Bbed0e63cD2392F503b135F5`.\n\nThis PR also adds a `mentions` parameter to the `stacked_simulation` job, which defaults to the current `S07K486JEH4` group. `stacked_simulation_sep` overrides it to `<!subteam^S07F1JJ80BW>`, and `stacked_simulation_eth` keeps the default.\n\n`src/script/check-task-statuses.sh` passes. With these two marked executed, no sep tasks are pending, so `stacked_simulation_sep` has nothing left to simulate.\n\nPrompted by: @mds1\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-15T16:46:30Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-15T17:32:55Z",
